> I opened a container of raw meatballs and had them in the fridge for a couple days. Now they've gone from redish to brown, but I thought they could last a week in the fridge. Is it okay to cook up?
**assistant**:
> If the meatballs have changed color from reddish to brown, it could be due to oxidation, which is normal when meat is exposed to air. However, the key things you should consider are smell and texture. If the meatballs have an off odor or feel slimy, it's better not to consume them, as these are signs of spoilage.
> 
> In general, raw ground meat can last in the fridge for 1-2 days. Since it's been a couple of days, you are right at the edge of this window.
> 
> To be absolutely safe, if you have any doubts, it might be best to err on the side of caution and not consume them. Food safety is important to prevent any risk of foodborne illness. If they smell fine and aren't slimy, ensure they are cooked thoroughly to an internal temperature of 160°F (71°C) to kill any potential bacteria.
